---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Observe written references to exact Cargo package IDs in a prepared native world

Usage: pse inspect dependency-usage [OPTIONS] <PACKAGE_IDS>...

Arguments:
  <PACKAGE_IDS>...  Source-qualified Cargo IDs (use inspect dependency to resolve names first)

Options:
  -C <checkout>
      --project <PROJECT>    Analyze a separately prepared project while retaining this checkout's session owner
      --backend <BACKEND>    [default: native-snapshot] [possible values: lsp, native-snapshot]
      --format <FORMAT>      Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --features <FEATURES>
      --fields <FIELDS>      Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices
      --budget <BUDGET>      Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts
      --no-default-features
      --target <TARGET>
      --test-context
      --build-macros
  -h, --help                 Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Observe written references to exact Cargo package IDs in a prepared native world

Usage: pse inspect dependency-usage [OPTIONS] <PACKAGE_IDS>...

Arguments:
  <PACKAGE_IDS>...
          Source-qualified Cargo IDs (use inspect dependency to resolve names first)

Options:
  -C <checkout>


      --project <PROJECT>
          Analyze a separately prepared project while retaining this checkout's session owner

      --backend <BACKEND>
          Possible values:
          - lsp:             The explicitly prepared reusable rust-analyzer LSP session
          - native-snapshot: An explicitly prepared immutable compatible-family HIR/IDE snapshot

          [default: native-snapshot]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --features <FEATURES>


      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts

      --no-default-features


      --target <TARGET>


      --test-context


      --build-macros


  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
